# Current game design

## Hero
- Theme: World of Warcraft, Horde side. Title prints `=== FOR THE HORDE ===`.
- A typed name is kept. Enter at the name prompt picks one name from `HERO_NAMES`.
- Starts with HP 30, XP 0, Gold 0, wins 0, level 1. The weapon is a random Poor (+0) or Common (+1) Club, Sword, or Mace. Poor is a d100 of 1-60. Common is 61-100.
- `attack_bonus` is the equipped weapon. `fight()` also adds `(level - 1) // 2`.
- Level comes from total XP and does not spend XP. Totals: level 2 at 50, then 100, 200, 400, and so on. Each level above 1 adds 5 max HP.
- Named Rare (+2) and Epic (+3) weapons are boss drops only. Doomhammer is Epic.

## Monsters (`MONSTERS`)
Each has `taunt`, `ac`, `damage`, and `xp`. Loot is stored in `ASSIGNED_LOOT`, not on the monster.
The boss is the separate `BOSS` dictionary, not a member of `MONSTERS`. `fight` picks the boss when `wins` is a positive multiple of 3.

| Monster | AC | Damage | XP |
|---|---|---|---|
| Goblin | 8 | 4 | 20 |
| Skeleton | 10 | 5 | 30 |
| Orc | 13 | 7 | 50 |
| Mimic | 11 | 6 | 40 |
| Human Footman | 9 | 4 | 25 |
| Night Elf Sentinel | 11 | 5 | 35 |
| Dwarf Mountaineer | 12 | 6 | 45 |
| Warchief of the Alliance (boss) | 16 | 8 | 80 |

## Loot (`LOOT`, `assign_loot`, `roll_loot`)
- Tiers follow WoW item quality: Poor, Common, Uncommon, Rare, Epic.
- `assign_loot()` runs once in `main()`. It stores each monster's Uncommon gear in `ASSIGNED_LOOT`.
- `roll_loot()` runs after a normal win. Roll = d100 + (monster AC - 8). Under 31 drops nothing. Poor and Common drop a generated weapon. Uncommon drops the assigned gear. A Rare or Epic roll on a normal monster drops Uncommon gear instead.
- A boss kill rolls one more d100: 1-70 nothing, 71-90 a Rare named weapon, 91-100 an Epic named weapon. The weapon goes in the bag.
- min_roll / gold value: Poor 31/1, Common 61/5, Uncommon 81/20, Rare 94/60, Epic 100/200.

## Shop
- Menu option 6. Options 1-4 stay as they are.
- A potion costs 15 gold and restores 10 HP, capped at max HP.
- Two weapons are rolled for the visit. Levels 1-2 are Poor and cost 20. Level 3 and up are Common and cost 50. Buying one equips it and sets `attack_bonus` to that weapon only.

## Save file (`saves/checkpoint.txt`)
- One `key=value` per line.
- `name` and `weapon` are strings. `bag` is a string joined with `|`. Everything else is an int.
- `load_checkpoint` returns only the keys in the file. After Continue, `fill_hero` fills weapon, attack bonus, bag, wins, level, and max HP when an old save is missing them.

## Menu
1 Fight, 2 View hero, 3 Save, 4 Quit, 5 View loot bag, 6 Visit the shop, 7 Rest, 8 Read battle log, 9 Load a hero.

The menu prints three labels across, with four spaces between columns. Reading order is left to right.

Continue with no `saves/checkpoint.txt` starts a new hero. Option 7 Rest heals 10 HP, and HP never goes above max HP. Option 8 prints `saves/battle_log.txt`. A fight prints one random room line before the taunt. Every fight then writes `saves/checkpoint.txt`. There is no y/n save question. Option 3 also writes `saves/<hero>.txt` (spaces removed from the name) and records that file in `saves/heroes.txt`. Option 9 loads one of those hero files.

A hit in the battle log reads `Name was hit by the Monster for N damage.` If that hit drops HP to 0 or below, the next log line is `Name collapsed and woke up back at camp.` HP is set back to max HP before the auto-save.
